    "['mpls ldp', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ldp', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ldp\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you need the exact equivalent in Juniper's configuration hierarchy format (where `mpls ldp` enables LDP globally), it would be:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ldp interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper's LDP implementation requires enabling it on interfaces explicitly (or using `interface all` as a shorthand). The Huawei command `mpls ldp` in the global context is roughly equivalent to enabling LDP globally in Juniper, but with interface associations.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface all', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ldp interface all', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ldp\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, if you need the exact equivalent in Juniper's configuration hierarchy format (where `mpls ldp` enables LDP globally), it would be:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ldp interface all\\n##\\n\\nNote: Juniper's LDP implementation requires enabling it on interfaces explicitly (or using `interface all` as a shorthand). The Huawei command `mpls ldp` in the global context is roughly equivalent to enabling LDP globally in Juniper, but with interface associations.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp interface all'}]]": 1,
