    "['mpls ldp', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface all', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the `mpls ldp` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ldp interface all\\nset protocols ldp interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper requires explicit interface declarations for LDP. \"interface all\" enables LDP on all interfaces, while \"lo0.0\" specifically enables it on the loopback (equivalent to Huawei\\'s implicit LDP enablement on configured interfaces).\\n2. Unlike Huawei where `mpls ldp` is a single command that enables LDP globally, Juniper separates the global enablement and interface-level configurations.\\n3. The IPv4 family is implicit in Juniper\\'s LDP implementation, unlike Huawei which requires explicit declaration.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp interface all'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ldp interface lo0.0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the equivalent Juniper configuration for the `mpls ldp` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ldp interface all\\nset protocols ldp interface lo0.0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. Juniper requires explicit interface declarations for LDP. \"interface all\" enables LDP on all interfaces, while \"lo0.0\" specifically enables it on the loopback (equivalent to Huawei\\'s implicit LDP enablement on configured interfaces).\\n2. Unlike Huawei where `mpls ldp` is a single command that enables LDP globally, Juniper separates the global enablement and interface-level configurations.\\n3. The IPv4 family is implicit in Juniper\\'s LDP implementation, unlike Huawei which requires explicit declaration.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ldp interface lo0.0'}]]": 1,
